@using HockeyPractice.Infrastructure
@model DrillCard
@*
    How long a drill runs, and where that number came from when a plan lengthened it.

    Rendered in four places (the plan page's running order and its drill cards, and the same two
    on the print sheet), which is why it is a partial: the breakdown has to say the same thing on
    the bench sheet as it does on the phone, and four copies of this markup would not stay that way.

    The CALLER decides what an unknown time looks like, because the four places disagree: the
    running order prints a dash, a drill card on screen shows nothing at all, and the print card
    says "no time set". So this renders only the known case and is asked for only inside an
    `is int` check.
*@
@{
    var mins = Model.EffectiveRunTimeMinutes ?? 0;
}
@RunTime.Human(mins)@if (Model.ShowsAddedTime)
{<span class="hp-time-breakdown"> (@RunTime.Human(Model.BaseRunTimeMinutes!.Value) <span class="hp-time-added">+ @RunTime.Human(Model.ExtraRunTimeMinutes!.Value)</span>)</span>}
